vpinos-core (1.1.25) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Launching from SSH works again: vpinos-launch run over SSH (for
    example `vpinos-launch vpinball /opt/vpinball/VPinballX_BGFX -play
    <table>`) stops the console on the cabinet for the run and starts it
    again afterwards, returning to the menu. Since the switch to the
    kmscon console, the console kept the screen and the program failed
    to start.
  * Programs no longer start too early after an earlier launch was
    stopped: vpinos-launch now waits for its own Hyprland instead of
    any leftover from a previous run, which could make VPinball fail
    with "wayland not available".

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:02:49 -0600

vpinos-core (1.1.24) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New Setup > GPU Driver option: NVIDIA legacy, NVIDIA's 580 driver
    for GTX 750 to 10-series and Titan V cards (Maxwell, Pascal, Volta),
    which the NVIDIA proprietary driver no longer supports. Like the
    proprietary driver it switches on the next launch, without a
    reboot, and Secure Boot must be off. VR with it encodes on the
    CPU: hardware encoding (NVENC) needs the proprietary driver.
  * NVIDIA proprietary is now described as for RTX 20/GTX 16 and newer.
  * System Info shows which NVIDIA driver is loaded.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:28:58 -0600

vpinos-core (1.1.23) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New Tools > Pinscape-Cross: opens Pinscape-Cross, the configuration
    and firmware tool for Pinscape Pico controller boards, in a window.
    It's installed the first time you pick it (up to about 180 MB with
    the libraries it needs, needs internet). amd64 only.
  * Tools > Reset Saved Settings is now option 5.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:46:53 -0600

vpinos-core (1.1.22) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Tools > VPX Editor now opens maximized, filling the screen,
    instead of as a small window in the middle.
  * VPX Editor now runs on Wayland directly instead of through X11.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:01:31 -0600

vpinos-core (1.1.21) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New Tools > vpxtool: opens a command prompt in the tables folder
    with vpxtool, a command-line tool for .vpx files (table info, ROM
    name, checking, extracting and comparing the script). It's
    installed the first time you pick it (about 6 MB, needs internet).
  * Tools > Reset Saved Settings is now option 4.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:25:35 -0600

vpinos-core (1.1.20) trixie; urgency=medium

  * VR > Setup > Install VR components now shows "installed" as soon
    as it finishes, without backing out of the menu. Other menu values
    (like VPX Editor) also refresh after their action runs.
  * VR > "Pair new headset" no longer says "(Wi-Fi)": pairing with a
    PIN is needed for USB headsets too.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 09:06:07 -0600

vpinos-core (1.1.19) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Launch VPinball Example Table works again. Newer VPinball builds
    ship the example table as exampleTable.vpz instead of
    exampleTable.vpx, so the menu failed with "cp: cannot stat".

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 08:05:55 -0600

vpinos-core (1.1.18) trixie; urgency=medium

  * DOF and other USB cabinet hardware (FTDI/serial boards, Pinscape,
    Teensy, Arduino) now work in VPinball without adding udev rules by
    hand.
  * ModemManager is turned off. It's only for cellular modems, and it
    briefly grabbed the serial port of DOF boards when they were
    plugged in. `sudo systemctl unmask ModemManager` turns it back on.

 -- Superhac <superhac007@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:06:13 -0500

